From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wsa883x: hand the PA gain over to DRE after
 unmute

With the compander (COMP) port in use, the codec's compander raises quiet
signals and sends the matching attenuation over that port for the amplifier's
dynamic range enhancement (DRE) to apply. The amplifier only applies it in DRE
mode, i.e. with DRE_CTL_1[0] cleared.

The driver sets that bit (gain from CSR) on unmute and only clears it on mute,
so during playback the PA runs at the fixed CSR gain and the compander's boost
reaches the speaker unbalanced. On a Huawei MateBook E Go (two WSA8835,
compander on at both ends), a 1 kHz tone swept over 39 dB comes out over only
22 dB, quiet signals 14.5 dB too loud, and any bass content pulls the rest of
the spectrum down by 7 to 14 dB.

Clear the bit 3 ms after enabling the PA, as the downstream driver does after
PA on. Measured on the same machine with the bit cleared during playback, the
sweep comes out over 34 dB and bass moves the rest by less than 4 dB.

Fixes: cdb09e623143 ("ASoC: codecs: wsa883x: add control, dapm widgets and map")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wsa883x.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa883x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa883x.c
index 468d2b38a..4d812f879 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa883x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa883x.c
@@ -1381,6 +1381,7 @@ static int wsa883x_set_sdw_stream(struct snd_soc_dai *dai,
 static int wsa883x_digital_mute(struct snd_soc_dai *dai, int mute, int stream)
 {
 	struct snd_soc_component *component = dai->component;
+	struct wsa883x_priv *wsa883x = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
 
 	if (mute) {
 		snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WSA883X_DRE_CTL_1,
@@ -1396,6 +1397,19 @@ static int wsa883x_digital_mute(struct snd_soc_dai *dai, int mute, int stream)
 					      WSA883X_GLOBAL_PA_EN_MASK,
 					      WSA883X_GLOBAL_PA_ENABLE);
 
+		/*
+		 * With the compander port in use, hand the PA gain over to DRE
+		 * once the PA is up, as the downstream driver does 3 ms after
+		 * enabling it. The codec's compander boosts quiet signals and
+		 * sends the matching attenuation over that port, which the PA
+		 * only applies in DRE mode; left at the CSR gain, the boost
+		 * reaches the speaker as heavy compression.
+		 */
+		if (wsa883x->port_enable[WSA883X_PORT_COMP]) {
+			usleep_range(3000, 3100);
+			snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WSA883X_DRE_CTL_1,
+						      WSA883X_DRE_GAIN_EN_MASK, 0);
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
